        "position": 5,
        "title": "Keeps people from approaching. Well made product.",
        "text": "We adopted a Siberian Husky mix that didn't know what it meant to be petted. It took a very long time for her to come to accept and love being touched near her head area. The only reason I would put a muzzle on is because she doesn't like strangers coming up to pet her. People sometimes don't listen when you tell them not to come close, especially when it comes to their kids. \"Oh, she's so cute... \" Me - \"please don't pet her she doesn't like it...\". Then I have to pull her away while they keep coming towards her. \"Did you hear what I said! Don't try to pet her - I don't know how she will react!\" With the muzzle it is more obvious. When we first tried to put it on she got really excited, because she thought it was her collar, which means we're going somewhere! She quickly realized that it wasn't her collar/leash, so it was a bit difficult to get her to settle down. We are still working on her acceptance of the mouth guard. Size wise she has a snout length of 3.5\" and a snout circumference of about 10\", so I ordered a size L in the camo. The entire muzzle is made out of nylon including the camo section, so it is waterproof. The ventilated section is stiff enough where it won't collapse, but it's still bendable. It fits perfectly, but is at its max adjustment as indicated in the size chart. This muzzle is well made and light weight. Product is exactly as described and shown in the marketing pictures.",
        "rating": 5,
        "date": "January 18, 2024",
        "author": "I'm here",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AEI3KBM4DSN3OWNFERWNLVA25D3Q?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png",
        "helpful_votes": "3 people found this helpful"
      },
      {
        "position": 6,
        "title": "Exactly what you'd expect from the photo",
        "text": "I ordered this muzzle for specific reasons, such as during nail grooming as my big strong boy is noncooperative, to be used for a brief timeout when needed, and to prevent him from eating potentially parasite-infested matters when allowed to roam off-leash. It baffles me why the description would include it being \"drinkable\" since the meshed front will not allow free drinking, and I don't know anyone who bottle-feeds their dogs. Other than that, this XL muzzle fits my Great Pyrenees mix boy perfectly when ordered as the size chart suggested, especially the snout circumference near 10.25\". From the center between his eyes to the nose tip, he measures 5\" and this mesh muzzle still fits comfortably without being too tight, although he hates wearing any muzzle. I have other muzzles but tried this because of the over-the-head strap that prevents him from taking off as he does with other muzzle styles unless they're set uncomfortably tight. I didn't know how well it'd hold up, but during the unfair experiment on him, he couldn't take it off and accepted his fate resorting to sleep. I wasn't sure if the center mesh portion would hold up to his clawing but he didn't rip any and this design with solid sides seems to work better than all mesh muzzles. I gave him a big treat afterward as a reward for his cooperation. It works just as I had hoped from the looks of the muzzle, so I'm happy with the product.",
        "rating": 5,
